&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Us&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, we are on a mission to help build a better Internet. Today the company runs one of the world’s largest networks that powers millions of websites and other Internet properties for customers ranging from individual bloggers to SMBs to Fortune 500 companies. Cloudflare protects and accelerates any Internet application online without adding hardware, installing software, or changing a line of code. Internet properties powered by Cloudflare all have web traffic routed through its intelligent global network, which gets smarter with every request. As a result, they see significant improvement in performance and a decrease in spam and other attacks. Cloudflare was named to Entrepreneur Magazine’s Top Company Cultures list and ranked among the World’s Most Innovative Companies by Fast Company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, we’re not looking for people who wait for a polished roadmap; we’re looking for the builders who see the cracks in the Internet that everyone else has simply learned to live with. We value candidates who have the instinct to spot a &quot;normalized&quot; problem and the AI-native curiosity to create a solution using the latest tools. Our culture is built on iteration, leveraging AI to ship faster today to make it better tomorrow, while ensuring that every improvement, no matter how small, is shared across the team to lift everyone up. If you’re the type of person who values curiosity over bureaucracy, and that AI is a partner in solving tough problems to keep the Internet moving forward, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Available Location&lt;/strong&gt; - Lisbon, Portugal&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, we are on a mission to help build a better Internet. Today the company runs one of the world’s largest networks that powers millions of websites and other Internet properties for customers ranging from individual bloggers to SMBs to Fortune 500 companies. Cloudflare protects and accelerates any Internet application online without adding hardware, installing software, or changing a line of code. Internet properties powered by Cloudflare all have web traffic routed through its intelligent global network, which gets smarter with every request. As a result, they see significant improvement in performance and a decrease in spam and other attacks. Cloudflare was named to Entrepreneur Magazine’s Top Company Cultures list and ranked among the World’s Most Innovative Companies by Fast Company.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, we’re not looking for people who wait for a polished roadmap; we’re looking for the builders who see the cracks in the Internet that everyone else has simply learned to live with. We value candidates who have the instinct to spot a &quot;normalized&quot; problem and the AI-native curiosity to create a solution using the latest tools. Our culture is built on iteration, leveraging AI to ship faster today to make it better tomorrow, while ensuring that every improvement, no matter how small, is shared across the team to lift everyone up. If you’re the type of person who values curiosity over bureaucracy, and that AI is a partner in solving tough problems to keep the Internet moving forward, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do as a Digital Customer Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Digital Customer Engineer (DCE) is a trusted technical advisor and a core contributor to Cloudflare’s technical go-to-market strategy. Working as part of a pooled team, you will support Small and Medium Business (SMB) and Digital Native Business (DNB) customers across the complete customer lifecycle - from initial technical discovery and validation through onboarding, adoption. You will bridge technical strategy and business value by helping customers design fit-for-purpose Cloudflare architectures, realize measurable outcomes, and confidently expand their use of the Cloudflare platform. Sitting within the GTM organization and reporting to a Customer Engineering leader, you will operate against shared team and territory goals while using AI-assisted workflows, standardization, and automation to serve customers efficiently and consistently, at scale.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Validation: &lt;/strong&gt;Partner closely with Account Executives to lead technical discovery, capture business requirements, and map customer infrastructure to fit-for-purpose Cloudflare architectures and solutions. Define the scope, success criteria, and evaluation plans for Proof of Concepts (PoCs) and other technical validations. Deliver tailored technical presentations, architectural diagrams, and demonstrations that show how Cloudflare addresses specific performance, security, reliability, and developer-platform challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Adoption &amp;amp; Value Realization:&lt;/strong&gt; Guide customers through onboarding and adoption by developing structured success plans and architectural guidance tailored to their goals and environments. Serve as a trusted technical contact and help customers apply configuration best practices across use cases such as DNS migrations, Zero Trust rollouts, and WAF optimization. Partner with Account Executives and other Cloudflare teams to support customer health, manage risk, and identify opportunities for expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial Accountability &amp;amp; Expansion: &lt;/strong&gt;Contribute to shared team and territory targets tied to new business, customer adoption, retention, and account growth. Help customers deepen their use of the Cloudflare platform and identify relevant cross-sell and upsell opportunities based on customer goals and product usage. Contribute to customer value reviews that translate Cloudflare capabilities and adoption into measurable business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trusted Advisory: &lt;/strong&gt;Act as a trusted technical advisor throughout the complete customer lifecycle, building strong relationships with technical and business stakeholders. Provide guidance on architecture, security posture, developer platforms, AI control layers, and adoption strategy. Identify technical risks or adoption barriers early and recommend practical steps to improve customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Orchestration &amp;amp; Workflow Automation: &lt;/strong&gt;Leverage AI agents, Large Language Models (LLMs), and internal platforms to automate routine tasks such as RFP/Security Questionnaire responses, sandbox provisioning, basic telemetry monitoring, and internal/external documentation, reclaiming your time for strategic customer advisory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Enablement:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Enablement and other internal teams to design, build, and maintain reusable technical resources. Create and deliver demonstrations, workshops, architectural guidance, and technical documentation that improve consistency and accelerate customer adoption. Share knowledge and reusable assets with the wider team to continuously raise the organization’s technical baseline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Skills and Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education: An undergraduate or graduate degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience: Up to 1–5 years of professional experience in a customer-facing technical role, such as Sales Engineering, technical consulting, technical support, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architectural Mindset: Ability to understand, whiteboard, and clearly explain network, security, application, or developer-platform architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consultative Skills: Ability to understand customer needs, ask effective discovery questions, and translate technical capabilities into relevant customer and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial Mindset: An understanding of customer buying decisions, enterprise or technology sales cycles, and how technical value supports adoption, retention, and growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication: Strong presentation and stakeholder-management skills, with the ability to explain technical concepts clearly to both hands-on practitioners and business decision-makers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Portfolio Management: Ability to prioritize work, manage multiple concurrent customer engagements, and collaborate effectively within a pooled team environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Breadth: We do not expect every candidate to be an expert in every domain. Qualified candidates should demonstrate knowledge or experience in at least three of the following areas:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Internet Fundamentals: Understanding of how the Internet works, including TCP/IP, DNS, HTTP(S), SSL/TLS, APIs, and core networking concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security: Familiarity with areas such as Web Application Firewalls, Bot Management, firewalls, rate limiting, Zero Trust, and SASE.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance: Understanding of website and application performance concepts, including latency, caching, content delivery, and modern web protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI Proficiency: Familiarity with prompt engineering, AI-assisted research, scripting or log analysis, LLM usage, and workflow automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coding and Scripting: Experience with at least one language such as Python, JavaScript, Bash, Lua, or Go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developer Platform Fluency: Familiarity with APIs, SDKs, webhooks, cloud-native applications, infrastructure as code, CI/CD, or observability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity, initiative, and a demonstrated ability to learn new technologies quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Languages: Native-like fluency, both written &amp;amp; spoken, in English AND (Swedish OR Russian)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strongly Preferred Qualifications (The &quot;Good-to-Haves&quot;)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating reusable technical assets, such as demonstrations, code samples, technical documentation, reference architectures, or customer workshops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cloud providers such as AWS, Microsoft Azure, or Google Cloud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to modern application architectures, including serverless computing, containers, microservices, and APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of common application-security risks and mitigation strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with LLM orchestration, Retrieval-Augmented Generation architectures, or model-access controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with SMB or Digital Native Business customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role may require travel up to 20% to attend customer meetings, conferences, industry events, and in-person team collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;● For Portugal based hires: Estimated annual salary is between €43,000 - €67,000.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;2,0,0&quot;&gt;The final offer will be inclusive of time exemption, in alignment with the applicable law and collective bargaining agreements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p id=&quot;p-rc_6e8c7261705bda5d-20&quot; data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;citation-1 citation-end-1&quot;&gt;This role is eligible to earn incentive compensation under Cloudflare’s Sales Compensation Plan. The estimated annual salary range includes the on-target incentive compensation that may be attained in this role under the Sales Compensation Plan.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Equity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;This role is eligible to participate in Cloudflare’s equity plan.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;What Makes Cloudflare Special?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re not just a highly ambitious, large-scale technology company. We’re a highly ambitious, large-scale technology company with a soul. Fundamental to our mission to help build a better Internet is protecting the free and open Internet.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://blog.cloudflare.com/protecting-free-expression-online/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Galileo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;: Since 2014, we&#39;ve equipped more than 2,400 journalism and civil society organizations in 111 countries with powerful tools to defend themselves against attacks that would otherwise censor their work, technology already used by Cloudflare’s enterprise customers--at no cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cloudflare.com/athenian/&quot;&gt;Athenian Project&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;: In 2017, we created the Athenian Project to ensure that state and local governments have the highest level of protection and reliability for free, so that their constituents have access to election information and voter registration. Since the project, we&#39;ve provided services to more than 425 local government election websites in 33 states.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://1.1.1.1/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1.1.1.1&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;: We released&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://1.1.1.1/&quot;&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;1.1.1.1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; to help fix the foundation of the Internet by building a faster, more secure and privacy-centric public DNS resolver. This is available publicly for everyone to use - it is the first consumer-focused service Cloudflare has ever released. Here’s the deal - we don’t store client IP addresses never, ever. We will continue to abide by our&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/1.1.1.1/privacy/public-dns-resolver&quot;&gt; privacy commitment&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; and ensure that no user data is sold to advertisers or used to target consumers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Sound like something you’d like to be a part of? We’d love to hear from you!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Please note that applicants who progress to the offer stage of the interview process may be asked to attend an in-person interview within one of the Cloudflare Offices or Cloudflare Hubs.&amp;nbsp; More details about this will be available at that stage of the interview process.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This position may require access to information protected under U.S. export control laws, including the U.S. Export Administration Regulations. Please note that any offer of employment may be conditioned on your authorization to receive software or technology controlled under these U.S. export laws without sponsorship for an export license.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Cloudflare is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. &amp;nbsp;We are committed to providing equal employment opportunity for all people and place great value in both diversity and inclusiveness. &amp;nbsp;All qualified applicants will be considered for employment without regard to their, or any other person&#39;s, perceived or actual&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;race, color, religion, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, physical or mental disability, medical condition, family care status, or any other basis protected by law. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We are an AA/Veterans/Disabled Employer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Cloudflare provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities. &amp;nbsp;Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job. Examples of reasonable accommodations include, but are not limited to, changing the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. &amp;nbsp;If you require a reasonable accommodation to apply for a job, please contact us via e-mail at &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;hr@cloudflare.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; or via mail at 101 Townsend St. San Francisco, CA 94107.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
